FIGURE's patch 1 of 1 to imgui_rich_md (commit 427bcb17f8c467d0dc1869b04f8e99a6c7b0e45f).

rich_md.cpp decodes the images of a Markdown text with stb_image, from its own copy (imgui_rich_md/third_party/
stb_image.h, v2.29, compiled by its stb_image_impl.cpp with exported stbi_* symbols). FIGURE keeps one copy of stb_image
(third_party/stb, v2.30, compiled static in native/figure_image.cpp, PNG and JPEG only): the include now names
native/figure_rich_md_stb.h, which maps the two functions rich_md.cpp calls (stbi_load_from_memory, stbi_image_free) to
FIGURE's decoder. No second decoder, no stbi_* symbol exported from libfigure_native.a to meet a program's own
stb_image. Applied to third_party/imgui_rich_md/rich_md.cpp; checked by src/tests/figure_test_markdown.F90 (an image
from a PNG file drawn). FIGURE-specific: not for upstream.

--- a/rich_md.cpp
+++ b/rich_md.cpp
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@
 #include "backends/mermaid/rich_md_mermaid.h"
 #endif
 
-#include "third_party/stb_image.h"
+#include "figure_rich_md_stb.h"  // FIGURE's patch 0001: stb_image is FIGURE's (native/figure_image.cpp)
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <string>
